Package: fmriphysio
Type: Package
Title: Fast Design-Free Physiological Denoising for Functional MRI
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Bradley", "Buchsbaum", email = "brad.buchsbaum@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Removes physiological noise from blood-oxygen-level-dependent
    (BOLD) functional magnetic resonance imaging (fMRI) time series without
    requiring a task design. Following the logic of PHYCAA+ (Churchill and
    Strother (2013) <doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2013.05.102>), a fast
    temporal-difference energy map separates likely neuronal voxels from
    non-neuronal voxels such as vasculature and cerebrospinal fluid.
    Temporally predictable components are extracted from a low-rank subspace,
    retained when they load more strongly on non-neuronal than on neuronal
    voxels, and projected out of the data. Components are extracted by one-shot
    canonical autocorrelation analysis or, through the 'dipca' package, by
    dynamic-inner canonical correlation or principal component analysis (Dong
    and Qin (2018) <doi:10.1016/j.jprocont.2017.05.002>). A CompCor baseline
    (Behzadi et al. (2007) <doi:10.1016/j.neuroimage.2007.04.042>) and
    design-free quality-control metrics are included for comparison.
